WEBVTT

00:00:05.989 --> 00:00:08.690
Welcome to the final phase of our data
analysis in YAMOBI.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.637
Once we have saved our
file, we will learn how to

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:15.230
access it and generate
our first statistical results.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.430
Step 1.

00:00:17.785 --> 00:00:18.970
Recover the saved file.

00:00:20.135 --> 00:00:21.945
When opening YAMOBI
again, it is possible

00:00:21.946 --> 00:00:23.746
that the database does
not appear immediately.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.850
To load it, go to the menu of the three
lines on the upper left side.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.830
Select Open and look for your file.

00:00:31.555 --> 00:00:33.395
You can also find it quickly in the recent
tab.

00:00:34.779 --> 00:00:37.690
Once opened, you will see all the
information we previously recorded.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.370
Step 2.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.050
Data exploration and descriptive
statistics.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.150
Now we will focus on descriptive
statistics.

00:00:46.069 --> 00:00:49.310
In the top tool bar, select Exploration.

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:51.230
And then click on Descriptives.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.338
You will notice that
in the left panel a list

00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:54.979
appears with all the
variables we created.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.601
Step 3.

00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:57.665
Generate frequency tables.

00:00:58.499 --> 00:01:01.070
We will make an example with the natural
and legal variable.

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:04.690
Select it and click on the arrow to move
it to the variable square.

00:01:05.949 --> 00:01:08.510
In the right panel of the results,
a summary will appear.

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:11.390
First, verify the value n.

00:01:12.059 --> 00:01:16.170
This indicates the number of cases and
must mark 8, coinciding with our example.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.441
Although you see other
measures such as media or

00:01:19.442 --> 00:01:21.770
fashion, for now we will
focus on the basic distribution.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.110
Step 4.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:25.690
Interpretation of results.

00:01:25.691 --> 00:01:29.110
To better visualize the
data, mark the option

00:01:29.111 --> 00:01:31.550
frequency tables in
the configuration panel.

00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:35.590
Automatically, a table will be generated
that indicates to us, for example,

00:01:36.064 --> 00:01:39.170
that we count with 3 government
authorities or traditional structures,

00:01:40.319 --> 00:01:47.890
37.5%, 3 cooperative or community
companies, 37.5%, an indigenous NGO,

00:01:48.989 --> 00:01:56.370
12.5%, an indigenous organization,
12.5%, Step 5.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.910
Multiple selection variables analysis.

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:00.726
We can repeat this
process with the variables

00:02:00.727 --> 00:02:02.407
we create for the
defense of the territory.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:07.079
If we add land recovery,
we will see that 50%

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.449
of organizations, 4 of
8, perform this action.

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:15.910
By adding community surveillance or action
in front of mega projects, the table will

00:02:15.911 --> 00:02:19.030
be updated showing us how many
organizations respond positively to each

00:02:19.031 --> 00:02:21.890
category, allowing us a precise diagnosis
of their activities.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.690
Step 6.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:25.690
Information export.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.110
Finally, these tables are ready for your
reports.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.691
You just have to make
right click on the table,

00:02:32.692 --> 00:02:35.650
select copy and paste it in
a Word or Excel document.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:39.450
With this, you can do more detailed
analysis and presentations of your results.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.266
A very powerful tool
that we will explore now is

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.600
the creation of crossed
or contingency tables.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.800
Step 1.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:52.700
Table configuration.

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:57.720
To start, go to the upper menu and select
the option Frequency.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.920
Within this menu, we will click on
contingency tables, independent samples.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.272
This function allows us
to compare two variables

00:03:06.273 --> 00:03:08.280
simultaneously to find
relationships between them.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.080
Step 2.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.600
Variable selection.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.910
For our example, we will use
the variable natural, legal, select

00:03:16.911 --> 00:03:20.160
it and click on the arrow to
locate it in the grid of rows.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:24.300
Then we will take the variable community
surveillance for columns.

00:03:25.114 --> 00:03:28.700
Automatically, YAMOBI will generate a
crossed table with detailed information

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:32.580
about the relationship between the type of
organization and its actions related to

00:03:32.581 --> 00:03:34.460
territorial rights and the defense of the
land.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.540
Step 3.

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:37.669
Interpretation of results.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:39.960
Let's analyze the obtained data.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.080
In the case of the organizations
identified as government authority or

00:03:44.081 --> 00:03:47.159
traditional structures, we
observe that the three registered

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.720
organizations carry out
community surveillance actions.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:55.140
On the other hand, in cooperatives or
community companies, we see that two of

00:03:55.141 --> 00:03:57.740
them carry out these actions, while one
does not.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.420
Step 4.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.480
Use of analysis.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:07.260
This type of tables is essential when we
want to identify patterns or direct

00:04:07.261 --> 00:04:11.560
relationships between different variables
of our database, allowing us to make a

00:04:11.561 --> 00:04:14.000
much deeper analysis of the collected
information.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.500
As a final step, we will explore one of
the most powerful tools of YAMOBI,

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.100
the data filtering.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.079
Step 1.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.880
Access to the filter menu.

00:04:24.785 --> 00:04:28.024
This function is extremely
useful when we work with large

00:04:28.025 --> 00:04:31.080
volume of information and we
want to analyze a specific group.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.200
To activate it, go to the top menu and
select the filter option.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.300
Step 2.

00:04:38.505 --> 00:04:39.920
Creation of the filter formula.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:44.541
Suppose we want to analyze
only the organizations identified

00:04:44.542 --> 00:04:46.622
as authority of government
or traditional structures.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.400
For this, we must enter a formula in the
filter box.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.140
We will write the name of the variable
exactly as we created it.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.305
For example,
naturalization of a legal or

00:04:57.306 --> 00:04:59.066
legal low, respecting
capital and guidelines.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:02.820
Following this, we will place a double
sign of equal, equal equal.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.800
Step 3.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.900
Use of numerical codes.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.080
YAMOBI automatically assigns a number to
each category.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.040
In our example, the traditional
authorities correspond to number 3.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.660
When completing the formula with this
number, the software will automatically

00:05:16.661 --> 00:05:19.823
hide all the cases that do
not comply with this criteria,

00:05:19.824 --> 00:05:22.040
leaving only the information
that interests us visible.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:23.480
Step 4.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.600
Segmented analysis.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:29.397
With the active filter, any
analysis that we perform as

00:05:29.398 --> 00:05:32.040
frequency tables will be applied
only to the selected group.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.640
For example, we could discover that 100%
of organizations that are authority of

00:05:36.641 --> 00:05:40.160
government or traditional structures carry
out recovery processes of land.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.220
This capacity of segmentation is
fundamental for a diagnosis of the data.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.240
Step 5.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.320
Disactivate the filter.

00:05:48.285 --> 00:05:51.340
If you want to see the database again
complete to perform other analysis,

00:05:51.815 --> 00:05:54.600
simply return to the filter window and
delete the formula.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:59.880
By doing so, all cases will be available
again for frequency tables or contingency.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.540
Congratulations.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.560
With these steps, you already have all the
necessary tools to collect information

00:06:06.561 --> 00:06:11.760
effectively, structure your database and
perform statistical analysis to know

00:06:11.761 --> 00:06:14.040
thoroughly your organization or present
reports.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.920
They have learned from the basic
configuration to the use of frequency

00:06:18.921 --> 00:06:23.020
tables, crossed tables and the
segmentation of cases through filters.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.003
It is time that they
start this process and

00:06:26.004 --> 00:06:27.844
transform their data
into actionable knowledge.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:32.040
Remember that on the part of Paguanca and
the Lampa-Guanca team, we are at your full

00:06:32.041 --> 00:06:35.800
disposal to attend to any doubt or
difficulty that arises on the road.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.380
Go ahead and good luck!